 ## Required portable implementation
 1. HTTPS/WSS-only security profile with exact HTTPS Origin allowlist, CSRF binding for state-changing paths, host-only Secure/HttpOnly/SameSite session-cookie posture, HSTS/CSP target profile and bounded request/message/connection resources.
-2. Authentication-generation-bound session continuity with monotonic transport generation, server/client cursors, idle/absolute expiry and fail-closed revocation/reauth behavior.
+2. Authentication-generation-bound session continuity with monotonic transport generation, server/client cursors, idle/absolute expiry and fail-closed revocation/reauth behavior; terminal session states cannot be resurrected and portable in-memory state transitions must match the PostgreSQL transition guard.
 3. Digest-only single-use resume tokens bound to principal/session, authentication generation, transport generation, device digest and acknowledged sequences; atomic consume and rotation.
 4. Version/sequence/request-digest/idempotency-bound client commands with immutable receipts and conflict rejection. Transport admission does not itself execute a domain side effect.
 5. Monotonic mobile background checkpoints and deterministic RESUME_ALLOWED/CATCH_UP_REQUIRED/REAUTH_REQUIRED/EXPIRED derivation.
